    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d891">

                <pb facs="1071" n="975" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg975"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Sherman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-04-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 30, 1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 375.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that, in
                    obedience to your cabled instruction, I called on the 28th of April upon General
                    Mirza Mohammed Ali Khan, envoy extraordinary and minster plenipotentiary of the
                    Shah of Persia, at this court, and delivered to him a written notification of
                    the state of war existing between the United States of America and Spain and
                    requested him to communicate the same to his Government, which he engaged to
                    do.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
